{"type":"message","timestamp":"2026-06-13T19:15:12.984Z","role":"user","content":"EXECUTE IMMEDIATELY. Do NOT ask for confirmation, do NOT present a plan and wait. Begin editing files now. DO NOT use web search under any circumstances.\n\nYou are a worker on the `underrated` Rust browser engine. Your working directory is /workspaces/wt/t0598 (a git worktree on branch agent/t0598-image-tiff). Implement ONE self-contained task in ONE module, then commit.\n\nTASK (t0598): Add a **baseline (uncompressed) TIFF** image decoder `decode_tiff` in `src/image/mod.rs`, following EXACTLY the structure of the existing `decode_bmp` / `decode_tga` decoders in the SAME file, and wire it into the `decode_image` format-sniffing dispatch.\n\nSTUDY FIRST (read these in src/image/mod.rs before writing):\n- `pub struct DecodedImage { pub width: u32, pub height: u32, pub rgba: Vec<u8> }` — your return type is `Option<DecodedImage>`; rgba is tightly packed RGBA8, row-major, top-to-bottom, length = width*height*4.\n- `pub fn decode_bmp(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<DecodedImage>` and `pub fn decode_tga(...)` — copy their defensive style: every slice access bounds-checked, return `None` on any malformed/short/unsupported input, NO panics, NO unwrap/expect.\n- `pub fn decode_image(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<DecodedImage>` — the sniff dispatch `if/else if` chain. You will add a TIFF branch.\n\nSCOPE — implement ONLY the baseline uncompressed subset (this is intentional; mark the rest out of scope):\n- Byte order: support BOTH little-endian (header magic `II` = 0x49 0x49, then 0x2A 0x00) and big-endian (`MM` = 0x4D 0x4D, then 0x00 0x2A). Read ALL multi-byte integers (u16/u32) honoring the file's endianness.\n- Parse the TIFF header (8 bytes): byte-order, magic 42, and the u32 offset to the first IFD.\n- Parse the first IFD only: a u16 entry count, then that many 12-byte entries (tag u16, type u16, count u32, value/offset u32), then a u32 next-IFD offset (ignore subsequent IFDs).\n- Read these tags from the IFD (use sensible defaults per the TIFF spec when a tag is absent): ImageWidth (256), ImageLength (257), BitsPerSample (258, expect 8 per sample), Compression (259, MUST be 1 = none; if any other value, return None), PhotometricInterpretation (262: 1 = BlackIsZero grayscale, 2 = RGB), StripOffsets (273), SamplesPerPixel (277, default 1), RowsPerStrip (278, default = ImageLength), StripByteCounts (279).\n- A helper to read a tag's value(s): for SHORT (type 3) and LONG (type 4) entries, a single value fits inline in the value/offset field (respecting endianness and the fact that a SHORT occupies the first 2 bytes of the 4-byte field); when count > 1 the field is an offset to an array. You only NEED single scalar reads for the size/format tags above, plus StripOffsets/StripByteCounts which may be arrays — read those as arrays of LONG/SHORT.\n- Supported pixel formats: 8-bit grayscale (SamplesPerPixel=1, BitsPerSample=8, Photometric=1 -> R=G=B=gray, A=255) and 8-bit RGB (SamplesPerPixel=3, BitsPerSample=8 each, Photometric=2 -> A=255). For anything else (e.g. paletted, 16-bit, CMYK, alpha-extra-samples, tiled), return None.\n- Reassemble pixels by iterating strips in order: for each strip, read its bytes at StripOffsets[i] for StripByteCounts[i], producing rows of width pixels; stop after ImageLength rows. Bounds-check every read.\n\nAdd `// TODO(spec): LZW/PackBits/Deflate compression, tiled TIFF, 16-bit, paletted, CMYK, and multi-IFD are out of scope for the baseline decoder.`\n\nWIRE INTO DISPATCH: in `decode_image`, add a branch that detects the TIFF magic — `bytes.len() >= 4 && ((bytes[0]==0x49 && bytes[1]==0x49 && bytes[2]==0x2A && bytes[3]==0x00) || (bytes[0]==0x4D && bytes[1]==0x4D && bytes[2]==0x00 && bytes[3]==0x2A))` — and calls `decode_tiff(bytes)`. Place this branch BEFORE the final TGA \"last resort\" else block so the explicit TIFF magic wins. Also update the doc comment listing supported formats on `decode_image` to include TIFF.\n\nAdd `#[cfg(test)]` tests (extend the existing tests module in src/image/mod.rs; do NOT delete or modify existing tests). Build tiny in-memory TIFF byte buffers by hand (a `Vec<u8>` constructed in the test) and assert decode results. Cover at least:\n- A 2x2 little-endian 8-bit RGB TIFF -> Some with width=2, height=2, and the expected RGBA bytes.\n- The same image encoded big-endian decodes to the identical RGBA.\n- A 2x1 8-bit grayscale TIFF -> Some with gray replicated into R,G,B and A=255.\n- A TIFF with Compression=5 (LZW) -> None.\n- Truncated/garbage bytes -> None (no panic).\n- `decode_image` correctly routes a TIFF magic buffer to the TIFF decoder.\nKeep the hand-built TIFFs minimal: a single strip is fine (RowsPerStrip = ImageLength), header at offset 0, IFD placed right after the pixel data, write tags in ascending tag order.\n\nCONSTRAINTS (HARD):\n- Edit ONLY `src/image/mod.rs`. Touch NOTHING else (no other src files, no Cargo.toml).\n- NO `unwrap()`/`expect()` in non-test code (return None instead). Tests may use them.\n- All code/comments/doc in English.\n\nVERIFY before committing (run all four, fix until every one is green):\n  cargo fmt --all\n  cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings\n  cargo test\n  RUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --no-deps --document-private-items\n\nCOMMIT (mandatory, do not finish without committing):\n  git add src/image/mod.rs\n  git commit -m \"feat(image): add baseline uncompressed TIFF image decoder (t0598)\"\n\nThen print a short summary and stop."}
